+    """`accumulate_process_transfer(owned, ...)`, with the outputs written
+    into `owned`'s private arrays when donation is proven safe. Returns
+    `(new_ledger, blocker)`; `blocker is None` means the donation path ran
+    (the eleven `_OWNED_DONOR_FIELDS` arrays of the RETURNED ledger ARE the
+    donor's arrays; the two canonical process-total arrays are new on both
+    paths; the per-field Kahan temporaries are still allocated and
+    released inside the call -- see the section comment). Otherwise the
+    public allocating call ran and `blocker` names the reason truthfully.
