@@ -0,0 +1,419 @@
+"""Shared-storage S4 PRIVATE: one windowed water step pair -- pickup, an
+external transport callback, deposit -- in ONE frame.
+
+Not exported (no `__all__` entry, not imported by `maple.water`), no public
+flag on any public function. Adopted from the SYRUP-qualified reference
+runtime's paired transaction (`docs/shared-storage/adoption-plan.md`) with
+the ownership proofs tightened as listed under "MAPLE adaptations".
+
+Why: the sequential coupling (public pickup call -> transport -> public
+deposit call) makes the deposit call copy the post-pickup column (window,
+totals, base, deep metadata, prefix packets) and allocate a fresh ledger
+from its first accumulation, while the post-pickup column and ledger stay
+alive in the caller. Here the post-pickup column and ledger are created
+and consumed inside this function only: they are never returned,
+published, or handed to the callback, so the deposit phase may ADOPT them
+(structural ownership by scoping -- no escaped ownership token, no identity
+or reference-count inference) once their storage is PROVEN disjoint from
+every caller array by memory ranges.
+
+Contract (`_apply_windowed_pickup_transport_deposit`)
+------------------------------------------------------
+Inputs: the caller's ACCEPTED state `voxel_column` (C0), `active_layer`
+(A0), `water` (W0), `ledger` (L0), `sediment_availability` (V0),
+`initial_available_fraction`; `pickup_holder` -- a ONE-element list holding
+the pickup `WaterProcessDemand`, popped here (single-use handoff, so
+neither the caller nor this frame keeps the requested pickup alive through
+the callback); `between` -- the transport callback; the public step's
+keyword options. The holder and the callback are validated BEFORE the
+holder is consumed; the fixed-capacity policy is required first of all.
+
+Phase P: the PUBLIC step body (`windowed_step._apply_windowed_water_
+process_demand(..., _owned=None)`, i.e. exactly `apply_windowed_water_
+process_demand`) on (C0, A0, W0, L0, pickup demand): its validations
+(demand, class order, growth, namespace, availability pair), availability
+cap, begin, shared arithmetic, publication into a private result and
+`validate_water_process_result`. Then only the post-pickup column C_p,
+active layer A_p, ledger L_p, availability V_p and the accounting view are
+kept; the result object (with its post-pickup water, zero face flux,
+requested-removal reference and receipt) is released.
+
+Callback: `between(view)` with `view` a `PickupView` holding ONLY the
+actual removal per cell/class (borrowed; never written afterwards) and the
+class / scalar accounting reductions. It must return `(depth_m,
+mobile_kg, deposit_demand)` -- the depth and post-transport mobile pool of
+the deposit call's water and its `WaterProcessDemand`. Any exception
+(e.g. a transport rejection) propagates; nothing has been published and
+C0 / A0 / W0 / L0 / V0 / the deep store are untouched.
+
+Callback results: the new water is checked like `with_water`
+(`WaterState`, `resolve_operand_namespace` over the private post-pickup
+state, the new water and the initial available fraction,
+`validate_water_state`), then every returned array -- the water's and the
+demand's -- is refused if it shares storage with any private post-pickup
+array (column INCLUDING its opaque packet, window-cache totals and
+pending-journal buffers, active layer, availability, ledger).
+
+Phase D: the same shared body on (C_p, A_p, new water, L_p, deposit
+demand, V_p) with an internal owner: the working bed is adopted from C_p
+(`windowed_transfer._begin_owned_windowed_transaction`, every public begin
+rule) ONLY after the owner proves that no C_p storage overlaps a caller
+array (public copying begin otherwise), the first ledger accumulation
+donates into L_p when `_accumulate_water_transfer_into_owned` proves it
+(caller ledger L0 plus every caller, borrowed and callback array in the
+foreign set; exact allocating fallback otherwise), and the second
+accumulation donates into the first's private result under the same
+guard. Stage-9 publication and `validate_water_process_result` are
+unchanged; deep-store writes remain the caller's later publication.
+
+Returns `(view, deposit_result)`: the pickup view and the PUBLIC
+`WindowedWaterProcessResult` of the deposit phase (bound to the caller's
+deep-store version, pending journal, exactly as the sequential deposit
+call's); its receipt's `paired_transaction` entry records truthfully what
+the owner did (begin mode, each accumulation donated or the fallback
+reason).
+
+MAPLE adaptations of the reference
+----------------------------------
+* Storage enumeration covers the OPAQUE holders the generic backend walker
+  omits, for the caller state, the private state and the callback arrays
+  alike: the prefix packets' `packet` AND every array of their E1
+  `PrefixPacketBinding` (the bound packet identity, the bound base
+  identity and the separate frozen `encoded_base` copy), the window
+  cache's totals AND its bound window array, the pending journal's three
+  host arrays and the binding's bound arrays, the exchange receipt's
+  journal. An unknown or malformed holder/binding FAILS CLOSED
+  (`PairedTransactionError`), never "safe by omission" (S4 correction 1:
+  Codex's reproducer showed a candidate column whose `base` was the
+  caller's hidden `encoded_base` being adopted and its flags changed).
+* Overlap is decided per array NAMESPACE (`array_namespace`) and memory
+  range (`arrays_share_memory`), never by exact Python type: an ndarray
+  subclass or a view sharing a caller buffer is caught.
+* The fixed-capacity policy and the S2 class-order / availability-pair
+  preflights run before any owned mutation (the owned deposit's
+  availability is the owner-held V_p, validated by the shared body).
+* An owned mutation may invalidate the PRIVATE post-pickup column's
+  bindings (its cache/packet objects die with it); it never touches a
+  caller-retained packet, cache or journal, which the overlap proof
+  guarantees and the tests pin.
+* The ledger donation uses the one shared `_kahan_add`; no compiled
+  in-place kernel is adopted, so the replacement values are still
+  computed as TEMPORARY arrays and then copied into the donor's eleven
+  arrays: what the donation saves is the RETAINED third ledger (the
+  returned arrays are the donor's), not the per-field temporaries, and a
+  helper call is measurably slower than the allocating public call (Codex
+  microprobe, 64x64x2 NumPy: traced new-byte peak 985,960 B owned versus
+  1,389,600 B public, 0.889 ms versus 0.692 ms). Every pending fold is
+  derived from the current `N_LEDGER_PROCESSES` channels.
+"""
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import dataclasses
+from dataclasses import dataclass
+from typing import Any
+
+from maple.core.backend import (
+    array_leaves,
+    array_namespace,
+    arrays_share_memory,
+    is_array,
+    resolve_operand_namespace,
+)
+from maple.core.types.voxel import ArrayBinding, VoxelWindowCache, WindowedVoxelColumnState
+from maple.core.types.water import WaterState
+from maple.surface.voxels.deep_store import DEFAULT_MAX_JOURNAL_RECORDS
+from maple.surface.voxels.windowed_inventory import require_fixed_windowed_capacity
+from maple.surface.voxels.windowed_pending import PendingDeepBinding
+from maple.surface.voxels.windowed_prefix import WindowedPrefixPackets
+from maple.surface.voxels.windowed_transfer import (
+    DEFAULT_EXCHANGE_GATHER_COLUMNS,
+    _begin_owned_windowed_transaction,
+)
+from maple.water.interfaces import WaterProcessDemand
+from maple.water.validation import validate_water_state
+from maple.water.windowed_step import (
+    _OWNER_HELD,
+    WindowedExchangeReceipt,
+    WindowedWaterProcessResult,
+    _apply_windowed_water_process_demand,
+)
+
+#: Accounting fields of the pickup result exposed to the callback (no state object, no donor array).
+PICKUP_VIEW_FIELDS = ("actual_removal_by_cell_class_kg", "requested_removal_by_class_kg",
+                      "actual_removal_by_class_kg", "availability_shortfall_by_class_kg", "shortfall_by_class_kg",
+                      "numerical_residual_by_class_kg", "numerical_residual_scalar_kg")
+
+
+class PairedTransactionError(ValueError):
+    """A paired-transaction contract refusal (handoff, callback result shape/type or aliasing)."""
+
+
+def _bound_array(binding: Any, what: str) -> Any:
+    """The array an `ArrayBinding` identity names; an unknown holder or a
+    non-array fails closed."""
+    if not isinstance(binding, ArrayBinding) or not is_array(binding.array):
+        raise PairedTransactionError(f"{what}: unknown or malformed array binding; ownership cannot be proven")
+    return binding.array
+
+
+def _prefix_packet_arrays(packets: Any) -> list:
+    """EVERY array a prefix-packet holder retains: the packet grid, the
+    E1 binding's bound packet identity, its bound base identity and its
+    separate frozen `encoded_base` copy. The holder and the binding types
+    are required by name; anything else fails closed."""
+    if not isinstance(packets, WindowedPrefixPackets) or not is_array(packets.packet):
+        raise PairedTransactionError("height_packet: unknown or malformed prefix-packet holder; ownership cannot "
+                                     "be proven")
+    try:
+        from maple.core.backend.prefix_cell_reductions import PrefixPacketBinding
+    except ImportError as exc:  # the E1 module is required for any column that carries packets
+        raise PairedTransactionError(f"height_packet: the prefix binding type is unavailable ({exc})") from exc
+    binding = packets.binding
+    if not isinstance(binding, PrefixPacketBinding) or not is_array(binding.encoded_base):
+        raise PairedTransactionError("height_packet.binding: unknown or malformed prefix binding; ownership cannot "
+                                     "be proven")
+    return [packets.packet, _bound_array(binding.packet, "height_packet.binding.packet"),
+            _bound_array(binding.base, "height_packet.binding.base"), binding.encoded_base]
+
+
+def _window_cache_arrays(cache: Any) -> list:
+    if not isinstance(cache, VoxelWindowCache) or not is_array(cache.window_totals_kg):
+        raise PairedTransactionError("window_cache: unknown or malformed window cache; ownership cannot be proven")
+    return [cache.window_totals_kg, _bound_array(cache.binding, "window_cache.binding")]
+
+
+def _pending_binding_arrays(pending: Any) -> list:
+    if not isinstance(pending, PendingDeepBinding):
+        raise PairedTransactionError("pending_deep: unknown or malformed pending binding; ownership cannot be proven")
+    journal = pending.journal
+    arrays = [journal.cell_flat, journal.voxel, journal.values_kg, *pending.arrays]
+    if not all(is_array(a) for a in arrays):
+        raise PairedTransactionError("pending_deep: a bound buffer is not an array; ownership cannot be proven")
+    return arrays
+
+
+@dataclass(frozen=True, eq=False)
+class PickupView:
+    """What the transport callback may see of the pickup phase: the ACTUAL
+    removal per cell/class (borrowed) and the accounting reductions -- never
+    a column, ledger, active layer, availability or water object."""
+
+    actual_removal_by_cell_class_kg: Any
+    requested_removal_by_class_kg: Any
+    actual_removal_by_class_kg: Any
+    availability_shortfall_by_class_kg: Any
+    shortfall_by_class_kg: Any
+    numerical_residual_by_class_kg: Any
+    numerical_residual_scalar_kg: Any
+
+
+def _opaque_storage(objects) -> list:
+    """Arrays held by the OPAQUE holders the generic walker omits, found by
+    walking dataclass trees / containers for windowed columns and exchange
+    receipts: the prefix packets with EVERY array of their E1 binding
+    (bound packet, bound base, frozen `encoded_base`), the window cache's
+    totals and bound window, the pending journal's arrays and the pending
+    binding's bound arrays, receipt journals. `seen` is traversal-only
+    bookkeeping over HOLDER objects (never over arrays): it avoids walking
+    one holder twice and infers nothing about ownership; every array a
+    holder names is listed, views included. An unknown holder type fails
+    closed."""
+    out: list = []
+    seen: set[int] = set()
+
+    def visit(obj: Any) -> None:
+        if obj is None or isinstance(obj, (str, bytes, int, float, bool)) or is_array(obj):
+            return
+        if id(obj) in seen:
+            return
+        seen.add(id(obj))
+        if isinstance(obj, WindowedVoxelColumnState):
+            if obj.height_packet is not None:
+                out.extend(_prefix_packet_arrays(obj.height_packet))
+            if obj.window_cache is not None:
+                out.extend(_window_cache_arrays(obj.window_cache))
+            if obj.pending_deep is not None:
+                out.extend(_pending_binding_arrays(obj.pending_deep))
+            return
+        if isinstance(obj, WindowedExchangeReceipt):
+            out.extend((obj.journal.cell_flat, obj.journal.voxel, obj.journal.values_kg))
+            return
+        if isinstance(obj, (tuple, list)):
+            for item in obj:
+                visit(item)
+            return
+        if isinstance(obj, dict):
+            for value in obj.values():
+                visit(value)
+            return
+        if hasattr(obj, "__dataclass_fields__"):
+            for field in dataclasses.fields(obj):
+                visit(getattr(obj, field.name))
+
+    for obj in objects:
+        visit(obj)
+    return out
+
+
+def _storage_leaves(*objects) -> tuple:
+    """Every array reachable from `objects`: the generic `array_leaves` walk
+    PLUS the opaque holders' buffers. Nothing is read or copied."""
+    leaves = [a for a in array_leaves(*objects) if is_array(a)]
+    leaves.extend(_opaque_storage(objects))
+    return tuple(leaves)
+
+
+def _overlaps(a, b) -> bool:
+    """Whether two arrays can share storage: same namespace (a different
+    backend cannot alias) and intersecting memory ranges (views and ndarray
+    subclasses included)."""
+    return array_namespace(a) is array_namespace(b) and arrays_share_memory(a, b)
+
+
+class _DepositOwner:
+    """Internal (never escapes this module's frame): the deposit phase's
+    adoption and donation rules, and the truthful record of what ran."""
+
+    __slots__ = (
+        "availability",
+        "begin_mode",
+        "caller_ledger",
+        "caller_state",
+        "column",
+        "first_blocker",
+        "foreign",
+        "ledger",
+        "second_blocker",
+    )
+
+    def __init__(self, column, caller_ledger, ledger, foreign, caller_state, availability):
+        self.column, self.caller_ledger, self.ledger, self.foreign = column, caller_ledger, ledger, tuple(foreign)
+        self.caller_state = tuple(caller_state)
+        self.first_blocker = "not run"
+        self.second_blocker = "not run"
+        self.begin_mode = "not run"
+        # The private post-pickup availability V_p (or None), held here instead of in the transaction frame or the
+        # deposit call's keyword arguments; handed over ONCE to the deposit body, which drops it after its last read.
+        self.availability = [availability]
+
+    def take_availability(self, placeholder):
+        if placeholder is not _OWNER_HELD:
+            raise PairedTransactionError("the owned deposit takes its availability only through the owner placeholder")
+        if not self.availability:
+            raise PairedTransactionError("the owner-held availability was already taken")
+        return self.availability.pop()
+
+    def begin(self, column, geometry, mass_resolution_kg, *, trust_window_cache, max_gather_columns,
+              max_journal_records, class_ids=None):
+        from maple.surface.voxels.windowed_transfer import begin_windowed_transaction
+
+        if column is not self.column:
+            raise PairedTransactionError("the owned deposit begin accepts only the transaction's private column")
+        kwargs = {"trust_window_cache": trust_window_cache, "max_gather_columns": max_gather_columns,
+                  "max_journal_records": max_journal_records, "class_ids": class_ids}
+        # Adoption only of storage the caller's state cannot reach (phase P made private copies): EVERY buffer the
+        # private column holds, the opaque packet / cache totals / pending journal included, is compared by
+        # namespace and memory range against EVERY caller buffer; any overlap takes the public copying begin
+        # instead -- identical bytes, the reason recorded.
+        adoptable = _storage_leaves(column)
+        if any(_overlaps(a, c) for a in adoptable for c in self.caller_state):
+            self.begin_mode = "copy: private column shares storage with the caller's state"
+            return begin_windowed_transaction(column, geometry, mass_resolution_kg, **kwargs)
+        self.begin_mode = "owned"
+        return _begin_owned_windowed_transaction(column, geometry, mass_resolution_kg, **kwargs)
+
+    def first_accumulation(self, ledger, process, actual_kg, residual_kg, mass_resolution_kg, *, foreign_arrays):
+        from maple.coupling.sediment_ledger.accumulate import _accumulate_water_transfer_into_owned
+
+        if ledger is not self.ledger:
+            raise PairedTransactionError("the owned first accumulation accepts only the transaction's private ledger")
+        new_ledger, self.first_blocker = _accumulate_water_transfer_into_owned(
+            ledger, self.caller_ledger, process, actual_kg, residual_kg, mass_resolution_kg,
+            foreign_arrays=tuple(foreign_arrays) + self.foreign)
+        return new_ledger
+
+    def second_foreign(self):
+        # After a donation the private post-pickup ledger's arrays ARE the working ledger's; otherwise (fallback) it
+        # is a separate live private ledger and joins the foreign set.
+        extra = () if self.first_blocker is None else tuple(array_leaves(self.ledger))
+        return self.foreign + extra
+
+    def record_second(self, blocker):
+        self.second_blocker = blocker
+
+    def describe(self) -> dict:
+        def outcome(blocker):
+            return "donated" if blocker is None else f"fallback (public allocating call): {blocker}"
+
+        return {"begin_mode": self.begin_mode,
+                "first_accumulation": outcome(self.first_blocker) if self.first_blocker != "not run" else "not run",
+                "second_accumulation": outcome(self.second_blocker) if self.second_blocker != "not run" else "not run"}
+
+
+def _apply_windowed_pickup_transport_deposit(
+    voxel_column, active_layer, water, ledger, pickup_holder, geometry, grain_classes, mass_resolution_kg, *,
+    between, sediment_availability=None, initial_available_fraction=None, adapter_name="prescribed",
+    detachment_integration="rate_times_dt", trust_window_cache=False,
+    max_gather_columns=DEFAULT_EXCHANGE_GATHER_COLUMNS, max_journal_records=DEFAULT_MAX_JOURNAL_RECORDS,
+):
+    """See the module docstring. PRIVATE; returns `(PickupView, WindowedWaterProcessResult)`."""
+    # Refusable before anything is consumed: the policy, the handoff shape and the callback.
+    require_fixed_windowed_capacity(geometry, operation="_apply_windowed_pickup_transport_deposit")
+    if not isinstance(pickup_holder, list) or len(pickup_holder) != 1:
+        raise PairedTransactionError("pickup_holder must be a one-element list (single-use handoff)")
+    if not callable(between):
+        raise PairedTransactionError("between must be callable")
+    if not isinstance(pickup_holder[0], WaterProcessDemand):
+        raise PairedTransactionError("pickup_holder must hold a WaterProcessDemand")
+    options = {"adapter_name": adapter_name, "detachment_integration": detachment_integration,
+               "trust_window_cache": trust_window_cache, "max_gather_columns": max_gather_columns,
+               "max_journal_records": max_journal_records}
+    # --- phase P: the public step, exactly ---------------------------------------------------------------------
+    result = _apply_windowed_water_process_demand(
+        voxel_column, active_layer, water, ledger, pickup_holder.pop(), geometry, grain_classes, mass_resolution_kg,
+        sediment_availability=sediment_availability, initial_available_fraction=initial_available_fraction,
+        _owned=None, **options)
+    view = PickupView(**{name: getattr(result, name) for name in PICKUP_VIEW_FIELDS})
+    column_p, layer_p, ledger_p = result.new_voxel_column, result.new_active_layer, result.new_ledger
+    availability_p = result.new_sediment_availability
+    del result  # post-pickup water, zero face flux, requested-removal reference, receipt: released before transport
+
+    # --- the external transport ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+    returned = between(view)
+    if not isinstance(returned, tuple) or len(returned) != 3:
+        raise PairedTransactionError("between must return (depth_m, mobile_kg, deposit_demand)")
+    depth_m, mobile_kg, deposit_demand = returned
+    del returned
+    if not isinstance(deposit_demand, WaterProcessDemand):
+        raise PairedTransactionError("between must return a WaterProcessDemand as the deposit demand")
+    # `with_water`'s checks of the new water, over the private post-pickup state
+    new_water = WaterState(depth_m, mobile_kg)
+    resolve_operand_namespace((column_p, layer_p, ledger_p, availability_p), new_water, initial_available_fraction)
+    validate_water_state(new_water, geometry.ny, geometry.nx, len(grain_classes.classes))
+    private = _storage_leaves(column_p, layer_p, ledger_p, availability_p)
+    callback_arrays = _storage_leaves(new_water, deposit_demand)
+    for a in callback_arrays:
+        for p in private:
+            if _overlaps(a, p):
+                raise PairedTransactionError("a callback-returned array shares storage with the transaction's "
+                                             "private post-pickup state; refused before any deposit work")
+    # The loop names would otherwise keep the LAST checked arrays alive through the deposit phase.
+    a = p = None
+    del private
+    # --- phase D: the same shared body with the internal owner ----------------------------------------------------
+    caller_state = _storage_leaves(voxel_column, active_layer, water, ledger, sediment_availability,
+                                   initial_available_fraction)
+    owner = _DepositOwner(column_p, ledger, ledger_p,
+                          _storage_leaves(voxel_column, active_layer, water, sediment_availability,
+                                          initial_available_fraction, view, *callback_arrays),
+                          caller_state, availability_p)
+    del caller_state
+    del callback_arrays
+    del availability_p  # now held only by the owner (taken by the deposit body)
+    deposit = _apply_windowed_water_process_demand(
+        column_p, layer_p, new_water, ledger_p, deposit_demand, geometry, grain_classes, mass_resolution_kg,
+        sediment_availability=_OWNER_HELD, initial_available_fraction=initial_available_fraction,
+        _owned=owner, **options)
+    if not isinstance(deposit, WindowedWaterProcessResult):  # defensive; the shared body returns this type
+        raise PairedTransactionError("deposit phase did not return a WindowedWaterProcessResult")
+    return view, deposit
